{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1368,
 "dur": 45.596,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Captain Rook robbed a treasure ship with a bucket of worms.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 2.659
  },
  {
   "text": "Inside the Golden Gull: ten thousand gold coins, and forty sleepy guards.",
   "s": 2.859,
   "e": 6.597
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Easy peasy, worm squeezy!\" Rook whispered, rowing under its shiny copper belly.",
   "s": 6.797,
   "e": 10.698
  },
  {
   "text": "First, his crew pried off the copper plates. Two thousand of them. With spoons.",
   "s": 10.898,
   "e": 14.396
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Rook dumped the worms on the bare wood. Sardine the cat only wanted one coin.",
   "s": 14.596,
   "e": 18.639
  },
  {
   "text": "A week later, the Golden Gull sagged, then sank slowly, like a cookie in milk.",
   "s": 18.839,
   "e": 22.603
  },
  {
   "text": "Ten thousand coins poured out the bottom, straight onto Rook's rowboat.",
   "s": 22.803,
   "e": 25.11
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Easy peasy,\" said Rook, as his wormy rowboat crumbled like a cracker.",
   "s": 25.31,
   "e": 28.662
  },
  {
   "text": "But why would a wooden ship wear copper underwear?",
   "s": 28.862,
   "e": 30.627
  },
  {
   "text": "Shipworms drill into wood and eat it, tunnel by tunnel, until the hull is a sponge.",
   "s": 30.927,
   "e": 34.851
  },
  {
   "text": "Copper is poison to them, so old ships wrapped their bottoms in it.",
   "s": 35.251,
   "e": 38.244
  },
  {
   "text": "So the gold sank, and a crab down there is now very rich.",
   "s": 38.444,
   "e": 41.024
  },
  {
   "text": "Rook paddled home in a copper bathtub. Sardine kept one coin.",
   "s": 41.224,
   "e": 44.296
  }
 ],
